    "body": "## Research (agent, M5): answering #655's open questions\n\n1. **Pin or re-implement? Pin, in stages.** SolidCraft's UI crates are built to be pinned by another app; that's solidcraft#14251's goal.\n   - **Pinnable today:** the token crates `solidcraft-theme` and `solidcraft-color` (plus `ui-text`, `ui-registry` and the viewport crates).\n   - **Not yet pinnable:** the components (`app_bar`, `ribbon`, `prefs_window`, `navigation_bar`, `history_bar`, `window_chrome`, `start_page`, `view_compass`). They still live in `solidcraft-ui-egui`. #14319 is merged, #14399 is open, and step 3 (extracting `crates/ui-kit`) is next.\n   - **Not on crates.io** (`solidcraft-theme` \"does not exist\" there). So the pin is a git dependency at a rev or tag. Re-implementing would drift and double the work.\n2. **egui / wgpu fit: a blocker today.** SolidCraft is on egui, eframe and egui-wgpu **0.37**, plus wgpu 30; CamCraft pins **=0.36.2**. One binary can't mix the two, so CamCraft bumps first: **#658**.\n3. **Layering and the command law hold.** Per #14399 the kit components \"take plain data and return what the user chose\". CamCraft keeps the ui → app → flecs rule by turning each returned choice into a command, as today's panels do. No kit component writes app state.\n4. **Mapping, as a first cut:**\n   - workspace tabs (`TabTable`) ↔ CamCraft's Setup / 2D / 3D / Drill / Turn / Multi-axis / Sim / Post groups;\n   - `history_bar` ↔ the operation list and undo history;\n   - the browser tree ↔ the setup and operation tree;\n   - `prefs_window` ↔ CamCraft's settings;\n   - `app_bar` / `ribbon` / `window_chrome` ↔ the main toolbar and window.\n5. **Icons:** the kit draws through a host-installed icon set (#14399), so CamCraft can keep its Tabler set (MIT) or adopt the kit's. That's a later sub-issue, decided with the components.\n6. **Snapshots:** every pixel golden changes. They're regenerated once at the cut that lands the theme (AGENTS.md), and the structural twins carry the asserts in the PRs.\n\n**Filed now:**\n- **#658:** egui 0.37 bump (prerequisite).\n- **#659:** theme tokens and tab accents from `solidcraft-theme` (the first visible step, pinnable today).\n\n**To file once solidcraft#14251 step 3 ships `solidcraft-ui-kit`:**\n- app bar, ribbon and window chrome;\n- the Preferences window;\n- tree and history mapping;\n- icons.\n\n**Questions for SolidCraft (nateuax or jyviko, Discord):**\n- (a) Which ref should an outside app pin: a tag per SolidCraft release, or a rev?\n- (b) Is there a timeline for #14251 step 3 (`crates/ui-kit`)?\n- (c) Will the vendored `egui-wgpu` patch be needed by a pinning app too?\n\nThis umbrella stays open until the post-#14251 sub-issues are filed.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
